{"step_index":100,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T22:44:50Z","model":"gemini-4-argon-high","input_tokens":2764,"cache_read_tokens":147127,"output_tokens":1105,"content":"I have translated the Python `statistics.quantiles` (`benchmark_quantiles`) program into a complete Lean 4 formalization at [31_statistics_quantiles.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/31_statistics_quantiles.lean).\n\n### Summary of Formalization\n\n1. **Functional Implementation ([31_statistics_quantiles.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/31_statistics_quantiles.lean#L24-L127))**:\n   - `pre`, `exclusiveClamp`, `inclusiveInterp`, `exclusiveInterp`, `quantilesGeneric`\n   - Exact rational model (`quantiles`, `benchmark_quantiles` over `ℚ`), floating-point execution layer (`quantilesFloat`, `benchmark_quantilesFloat` over `Float`), and real-number mathematical layer (`quantilesReal`, `benchmark_quantilesReal` over `ℝ`).\n2. **Unit Tests ([31_statistics_quantiles.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/31_statistics_quantiles.lean#L133-L202))**:\n   - All 9 test cases from Python's `check` (basic quartiles, deciles, median, inclusive method, exclusive method, larger dataset, unsorted input, fractional/float data, and error cases for `< 2` elements, `n < 1`, and invalid `method`), verified via `#eval` and `by native_decide` on both `ℚ` and `Float`.\n3. **Pre-condition & Properties ([31_statistics_quantiles.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/31_statistics_quantiles.lean#L208-L911))**:\n   - `Pre`: `data.length ≥ 2 ∧ n ≥ 1 ∧ (method = \"inclusive\" ∨ method = \"exclusive\")` (`pre_eq_true_iff`).\n   - `valid_iff_pre_prop` / `valid_iff_pre_thm` & `error_iff_not_pre_thm`: succeeds (`isSome`) iff `Pre` holds, and returns `none` otherwise.\n   - `length_prop` / `length_thm` & `float_length_thm`: output list has length `n - 1`.\n   - `sorted_idempotent_prop` / `sorted_idempotent_thm` & `perm_invariant_thm`: permutation and sorting invariance.\n   - `monotone_prop` / `monotone_thm`: output cut points are sorted in non-decreasing order (`List.Pairwise (· ≤ ·)`) for both `\"inclusive\"` and `\"exclusive\"` methods.\n   - `inclusive_bounds_prop` / `inclusive_bounds_thm`: for `\"inclusive\"`, every cut point lies between the minimum and maximum of `data`.\n   - `pointwise_prop` / `pointwise_thm`: exact pointwise linear interpolation specification for every index `k < n - 1`.\n   - `constant_data_prop` / `constant_data_thm`: constant datasets with value `c` produce `List.replicate (n - 1) c`.\n   - `shift_equivariant_prop` / `shift_equivariant_thm`: translation equivariance under `x ↦ x + c`.\n   - `benchmark_quantilesReal_ratCast_thm` & `benchmark_quantilesReal_spec_thm`: `ℚ`-to-`ℝ` cast correspondence and `ℝ`-layer specification.\n4. **Post-condition, PBTs, and Correctness Theorem ([31_statistics_quantiles.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/31_statistics_quantiles.lean#L917-L1121))**:\n   - `Post_prop` combining the verified properties, tested via both randomized Plausible checks (`#eval Plausible.Testable.check ...`) and bounded `native_decide` PBTs, and proved in `benchmark_quantiles_correct`.\n5. **Imperative Implementation & Equivalence ([31_statistics_quantiles.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/31_statistics_quantiles.lean#L1127-L1310))**:\n   - `quantiles_imp`, `benchmark_quantiles_imp`, `quantilesFloat_imp`, and `benchmark_quantilesFloat_imp` using `Id.run do` and mutable loop state, tested and proved equivalent to the functional implementations in `quantiles_equiv`, `benchmark_quantiles_equiv`, `quantilesFloat_equiv`, and `benchmark_quantilesFloat_equiv`."}
